# The URLs the built SPA may contain, read by scripts/check-dist-urls.sh. An entry ending in /*
# allows the URL and anything under it. A new entry is argued in review: the SPA calls nothing
# outside its own origin (docs/features/security.md section 3).

# The SVG namespaces.
http://www.w3.org/2000/svg
http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink
# The MathML namespace, which Vue's DOM runtime passes to createElementNS.
http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML
# The license header.
http://www.gnu.org/licenses/
# The license comment that Tailwind writes at the top of the CSS.
https://tailwindcss.com
# The reference link Vue's production runtime prints in a console warning; never fetched.
https://vuejs.org/error-reference/*
# The About screen's OpenSpeedTest snippet: a placeholder host the user replaces; never fetched.
https://ost.example.lan/*
# The About screen's source and documentation links, and the base-path error's link to the
# deployment guide.
https://github.com/leinardi/bitgauge/*
